    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Edward Jenner is known as the Father of Immunology for developing the smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "BCG (Bacille Calmette-Guérin) vaccine is given for Tuberculosis, while DPT protects against Diphtheria, Pertussis, and Tetanus.",
        "Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium and transmitted by female Anopheles mosquitoes.",
        "Innate immunity provides immediate, non-specific defense barriers (physical, chemical, and cellular)."
      ],
      "id": "fbkaliq"
